From: aurtxx <aurtxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] bootloader: deploy systemd-boot with ibt=off for Alder Lake

Intel Alder Lake (12th Gen) CPUs enforce Indirect Branch Tracking (IBT)
as part of Control-flow Enforcement Technology (CET). The gbOS86 kernel
(6.18.21-gbos-whl) contains KernelSU hook trampolines that lack ENDBR64
instructions, triggering a fatal kernel panic on the very first instruction
executed after EFI handover:

  Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception
  [    0.641882] Missing ENDBR: ksu_handle_init+0x0/0x10 [kernelsu]
  [    0.641885] Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception
  [    0.641888] CR2: 0000000000000000

The original gbOS86 bootloader was a unified kernel image (UKI) named
EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI with hardcoded kernel command-line parameters that
could not be modified at boot.

This change separates the UKI into:
1. systemd-boot (sd-boot x86_64) installed as EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI
2. The extracted kernel/initramfs payload stored as EFI/BOOT/KERNEL.EFI
3. A systemd-boot loader entry (loader/entries/gbos.conf) passing `ibt=off`:

--- a/loader/entries/gbos.conf
+++ b/loader/entries/gbos.conf
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+title gbOS86 (Alder Lake CET fix)
+linux /EFI/BOOT/KERNEL.EFI
+options ibt=off drm.panic_screen=kmsg
--- a/loader/loader.conf
+++ b/loader/loader.conf
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+timeout 3
+default gbos.conf
+console-mode max
+editor yes
